{"type":"text","timestamp":1791623250056,"sessionID":"ses_edaef49d5ffehLoopmZWUk3SS7","part":{"id":"prt_125113f5b0016lDAxTSaK27OB0","messageID":"msg_125110cb2001rMGPys4oJl420f","sessionID":"ses_edaef49d5ffehLoopmZWUk3SS7","type":"text","text":"`Search.svelte` (lines 60–78) is the sole inline search bar, used only from the shared library `Header.svelte`, which every library page renders. The root cause is clear: the absolutely-positioned container `<div class=\"absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center\">` spans the full header width and intercepts clicks across the button row. Let me check how a completed job's `tasks.md` is formatted, so I match the project's convention.","time":{"start":1791623249755,"end":1791623250052}}}
