{"type":"text","timestamp":1791623266495,"sessionID":"ses_edaef49d5ffehLoopmZWUk3SS7","part":{"id":"prt_1251176bb001FEe34Ev6WTJHEZ","messageID":"msg_125117192001dmXVXJGe4CxDWl","sessionID":"ses_edaef49d5ffehLoopmZWUk3SS7","type":"text","text":"`tasks.md` written. Summary of the analysis:\n\n## Branch check\nI could not verify the branch mechanically: `/workspace/.git` is not readable from this sandbox (`BadResource` on `.git/HEAD` — the same failure the earlier analyst attempt hit), and no shell tool is available for `git branch --show-current`. I proceeded per the mount contract (a job's mounted workspace is always its own job-branch worktree); if that assumption is wrong, stop here.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed in code)\n`src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte` opens the search as\n```svelte\n<div class=\"absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center\">\n```\n— a full-width, absolutely positioned, **transparent** container that floats above the header row rendered by `shared/Header.svelte`. It stays invisible but captures every click across the header, making the Filter/Releases/Recommender/genre/Create buttons unclickable while the search is open. `Search.svelte` is the only inline library search (all eight library pages share this Header). The separate `LibrarySearchModal` is a modal and unaffected. No render report/screenshots exist for this job.\n\n## Tasks written to `tasks.md`\n- **TASK-1** — In `Search.svelte`, make the overlay container `pointer-events-none` and the input + close button `pointer-events-auto`, so only the actual input area blocks clicks. *File:* `src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte`. *Depends:* none. *Risk:* low — one-file class-only change, no visual/logic/i18n impact.\n- **TASK-2** — Verify: `npm run check` + build, plus manual click-through of header buttons and ViewSwitcher at desktop/mobile widths with the search open; typing in the input must still work. *Files:* none. *Depends:* TASK-1. *Risk:* low — jsdom can't model pointer-event hit-testing, so this is a manual/visual verification.\n\nNotes captured for the developer: keep `w-full`/z-indices/input widths as-is (visual layout is intended); the width-constraint alternative was considered and rejected as more fragile; the magnifier-reopen no-op remains harmless. No new UI strings, so no i18n changes; no out-of-scope expansion.","time":{"start":1791623263931,"end":1791623266490}}}
