one` to the search-overlay container\n36:      (`absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center`) and `pointer-events-auto` to the\n37:      search input and to the close (circle-x) button, so only the actual input area\n38:      blocks clicks while the search is open and the rest of the header stays clickable.\n39:      files: src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte\n40:      depends: none\n41:      risk: low — one-file, CSS-class-only change; no visual or logic change, no new\n42:      UI strings (no i18n impact). Also closes the same click-blocking during the\n43:      collapsed/fade-in state (`w-0` input) for free.\n44: \n45: TASK-2: Verify the fix: run `npm run check` (+ `npm run build`) and manually confirm\n46:      that with the search open, the header buttons (Filter, Releases, Recommender,\n47:      genre edit, Create — desktop and mobile variants) and the ViewSwitcher remain\n48:      clickable on both sides of the centered input, at desktop and mobile widths,\n49:      and that typing in the input still works and blocks what sits behind it.\n50:      files: none (verification only — no code change expected)\n51:      depends: TASK-1\n52:      risk: low — verification task; jsdom cannot model pointer-event hit-testing, so a\n53:      component test would not genuinely validate the click-through, and no such test\n54:      exists for this component today.\n55: \n56: ## Notes for the developer\n57: \n58: - Do not change the container's `w-full`, the input widths, or the z-indices —\n59:   the visual layout is intentional (centered search bar over a full-width header).\n60:   The only required change is pointer-event behaviour.\n61: - An alternative (constraining the container width to the input's width) is a valid\n62:   approach but wider-reaching and more fragile across breakpoints (input `w-72` vs\n63:   `md:w-96` + the 30px close-button overhang); prefer TASK-1's pointer-events fix.\n64: - Re-opening the search by clicking the magnifier icon while the overlay is open is\n65:   a no-op and stays harmless after the change.\n\n(End of file - total 65 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte` renders its inline search input\ninside an absolutely positioned, full-width, transparent container:\n\n```\n<div class=\"absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center\">\n```\n\nWhen `library.searchVisible` is true, this container floats above the whole header\nrow (the same header that holds Filter / Releases / Recommender / genre-edit /\nCreate buttons, rendered by `libraries/shared/Header.svelte`). The container has no","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte` renders its inline search input\ninside an absolutely positioned, full-width, transparent container:\n\n```\n<div class=\"absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center\">\n```\n\nWhen `library.searchVisible` is true, this container floats above the whole header\nrow (the same header that holds Filter / Releases / Recommender / genre-edit /\nCreate buttons, rendered by `libraries/shared/Header.svelte`). The container has no\nbackground, so the buttons stay visible, but it intercepts every click across the\nheader width, making them unclickable — exactly what the brief describes.\n\n`Search.svelte` is the only inline search implementation for libraries (used only by\n`shared/Header.svelte`, which all eight library pages route through); the separate\n`LibrarySearchModal.svelte` is a modal and is not affected.\n\nFix: make the overlay container click-through (`pointer-events-none`) and restore\npointer events only on the input and the close button (`pointer-events-auto`). The\ninput itself keeps blocking clicks underneath it (with `inputExpanded`, `w-72` /\n`md:w-96`), which per the brief is the correct behaviour. Visual layout is unchanged.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: In `Search.svelte`, add `pointer-events-none` to the search-overlay container\n     (`absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center`) and `pointer-events-auto` to the\n     search input and to the close (circle-x) button, so only the actual input area\n     blocks clicks while the search is open and the rest of the header stays clickable.\n     files: src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — one-file, CSS-class-only change; no visual or logic change, no new\n     UI strings (no i18n impact). Also closes the same click-blocking during the\n     collapsed/fade-in state (`w-0` input) for free.\n\nTASK-2: Verify the fix: run `npm run check` (+ `npm run build`) and manually confirm\n     that with the search open, the header buttons (Filter, Releases, Recommender,\n     genre edit, Create — desktop and mobile variants) and the ViewSwitcher remain\n     clickable on both sides of the centered input, at desktop and mobile widths,\n     and that typing in the input still works and blocks what sits behind it.\n     files: none (verification only — no code change expected)\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — verification task; jsdom cannot model pointer-event hit-testing, so a\n     component test would not genuinely validate the click-through, and no such test\n     exists for this component today.\n\n## Notes for the developer\n\n- Do not change the container's `w-full`, the input widths, or the z-indices —\n  the visual layout is intentional (centered search bar over a full-width header).\n  The only required change is pointer-event behaviour.\n- An alternative (constraining the container width to the input's width) is a valid\n  approach but wider-reaching and more fragile across breakpoints (input `w-72` vs\n  `md:w-96` + the 30px close-button overhang); prefer TASK-1's pointer-events fix.\n- Re-opening the search by clicking the magnifier icon while the overlay is open is\n  a no-op and stays harmless after the change.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":65,"totalLines":65,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791623277719,"end":1791623277856}},"id":"prt_12511ac64001ExxvTfOVGULX1X","sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","messageID":"msg_12511a57f001i6W7N9nztbHM1y"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791623277882,"sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_IcIAqgwDYIHoxC4HlvF02645","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n2: \n3: id: lot\n4: developer:\n5: date:\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Summary\n10: \n11: <!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n12: \n13: ## Changes\n14: \n15: <!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n16: \n17: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n18: \n19: <!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->\n\n(End of file - total 19 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\ndeveloper:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n\n## Changes\n\n<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\ndeveloper:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n\n## Changes\n\n<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":19,"totalLines":19,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791623277772,"end":1791623277862}},"id":"prt_12511ac9b001K7ZE4IaxPQhoEt","sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","messageID":"msg_12511a57f001i6W7N9nztbHM1y"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791623277882,"sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_QuKZumZeVJcwYumlaULD6065","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/brief.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n2: \n3: type: fix\n4: id: lot\n5: branch: fix/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries\n6: date: 2026-10-10\n7: author: Leander Muskalla\n8: \n9: ## What\n10: \n11: In the libraries of solyto, if you open the search, the search bar itself is in the middle, but it's background container is full width. It's therefore on top of the buttons in the header. You when you searched for something, didn't find it and then maybe wanted to add something, you can't click the button even though it's in plain view.\n12: Where the search input is, it's correct that you cannot click buttons that might hide behind it. But otherwise, everything should be still clickable.\n13: \n14: ## Why\n15: \n16: <!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n17: \n18: ## Out of scope\n19: \n20: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n21: \n22: ## Notes\n23: \n24: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\n\n(End of file - total 24 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\ntype: fix\nid: lot\nbranch: fix/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nIn the libraries of solyto, if you open the search, the search bar itself is in the middle, but it's background container is full width. It's therefore on top of the buttons in the header. You when you searched for something, didn't find it and then maybe wanted to add something, you can't click the button even though it's in plain view.\nWhere the search input is, it's correct that you cannot click buttons that might hide behind it. But otherwise, everything should be still clickable.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/brief.md","text":"# Brief: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\ntype: fix\nid: lot\nbranch: fix/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nIn the libraries of solyto, if you open the search, the search bar itself is in the middle, but it's background container is full width. It's therefore on top of the buttons in the header. You when you searched for something, didn't find it and then maybe wanted to add something, you can't click the button even though it's in plain view.\nWhere the search input is, it's correct that you cannot click buttons that might hide behind it. But otherwise, everything should be still clickable.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n\n## Notes\n\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":24,"totalLines":24,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/brief.md","time":{"start":1791623277664,"end":1791623277867}},"id":"prt_12511aba3001Z5MRp2jBJHaXh8","sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","messageID":"msg_12511a57f001i6W7N9nztbHM1y"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791623277883,"sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_9e7O9A3Rqq8B8pGNsnoz3182","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n2: \n3: id: lot\n4: reviewer:\n5: date:\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Review\n10: \n11: <!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n12:      notes: ...\n13: \n14: TASK-2: ...\n15: -->\n16: \n17: ## Security\n18: \n19: <!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n20: \n21: ## Overall\n22: \n23: <!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n24: <!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\n\n(End of file - total 24 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Verdict: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\nreviewer:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\n<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n     notes: ...\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\n## Security\n\n<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md","text":"# Verdict: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\nreviewer:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\n<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n     notes: ...\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\n## Security\n\n<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n\n## Overall\n\n<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":24,"totalLines":24,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md","time":{"start":1791623277824,"end":1791623277874}},"id":"prt_12511acd1001Vpzm4JfC7blHlZ","sessionID":"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs","messageID":"msg_12511a57f001i6W7N9nztbHM1y"}}
