{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791624166757,"sessionID":"ses_edae0eac3ffeMK1M7G94zFEyN9","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_ET_HAlnP3QVYyNF04aiK4bf2337","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n2: \n3: id: lot\n4: developer: @developer\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: ## Summary\n8: \n9: Fixed the library search overlay intercepting clicks on the header buttons\n10: (Filter / Releases / Recommender / genre-edit / Create / ViewSwitcher) while\n11: the search is open. The overlay container in `Search.svelte` was\n12: `absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center` — a full-width, transparent layer\n13: floating above the header row. It had no background, so the buttons stayed\n14: visible, but it swallowed every click across the header width.\n15: \n16: The fix makes the overlay container click-through (`pointer-events-none`) and\n17: restores pointer events only on the search input and the close button\n18: (`pointer-events-auto`). The input itself still blocks clicks on whatever sits\n19: behind it (only `w-72` / `md:w-96` wide when expanded), which is the intended\n20: behaviour per the brief. Visual layout is unchanged.\n21: \n22: TASK-1: CSS-class-only change in `Search.svelte`.\n23: TASK-2: Verified via `npm run check` (0 errors / 0 warnings), Live\n24:   hit-testing with Playwright + headless chromium at desktop (1280px) and\n25:   mobile (375px) widths, and inspection of the built CSS.\n26: \n27: ## Changes\n28: \n29: TASK-1: `src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte`\n30:   - Search-overlay container (`div.absolute.z-30.flex.w-full.justify-center`,\n31:     renders when `library.searchVisible` is true): added `pointer-events-none`\n32:     so clicks pass through the full-width transparent container to the header\n33:     buttons underneath.\n34:   - Search `<input>`: added `pointer-events-auto` so the input itself stays\n35:     interactive (typing, focusing) and continues to block clicks on anything\n36:     directly behind its own footprint.\n37:   - Close button (`<IconCircleX />`, `ml-[-30px]` overhang): added\n38:     `pointer-events-auto` so it stays clickable.\n39:   - No change to `w-full`, input widths, z-indices, or any visual styling.\n40: \n41: TASK-2: Verification only — no code change.\n42:   - `npm run check` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n43:   - `npm run build` → the Vite transform + Tailwind CSS generation complete\n44:     (`✓ built`, all 1961 modules), and the generated app CSS contains both\n45:     `pointer-events-auto` and `pointer-events-none` utilities. The final\n46:     adapter-node output step is OOM-killed in this environment (2 GB cgroup\n47:     memory limit); this is a pre-existing environment constraint, unrelated to\n48:     the change (the changed files compile cleanly and the client build output\n49:     is produced).\n50:   - Playwright hit-test verification (replicating the exact Header + Search\n51:     overlay structure): with the overlay open at 1280px and 375px,\n52:     * Filter / Create buttons on both sides of the centered input receive\n53:       clicks (click propagates through the overlay container),\n54:     * the close button receives clicks,\n55:     * a button positioned directly under the expanded input does NOT receive\n56:       clicks (correct blocking behaviour),\n57:     * typing into the input works,\n58:     * computed `pointer-events` = `none` on the container, `auto` on input and\n59:       close button.\n60:   - `npm test`: 723/724 pass; the single failure is a pre-existing, unrelated\n61:     failure in `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts`\n62:     (`StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes` — expects a\n63:     `.bg-blue-50` class which Tailwind v4 does not generate as a static\n64:     utility; the assertion exists in HEAD, untouched by this job).\n65: \n66: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n67: \n68: - `npm run build` cannot complete the final adapter-node server output in this\n69:   environment due to a 2 GB cgroup memory limit (the process is OOM-killed\n70:   during app-wide chunk rendering). CI / machines with more memory complete\n71:   it. Not caused by and not addressable from this change.\n72: - Pre-existing test failure in `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts`\n73:   (`StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes`, expecting\n74:   `.bg-blue-50`) — unrelated to the libraries search bar; already failing\n75:   before this job.\n\n(End of file - total 75 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the library search overlay intercepting clicks on the header buttons\n(Filter / Releases / Recommender / genre-edit / Create / ViewSwitcher) while\nthe search is open. The overlay container in `Search.svelte` was\n`absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center` — a full-width, transparent layer\nfloating above the header row. It had no background, so the buttons stayed\nvisible, but it swallowed every click across the header width.\n\nThe fix makes the overlay container click-through (`pointer-events-none`) and\nrestores pointer events only on the search input and the close button\n(`pointer-events-auto`). The input itself still blocks clicks on whatever sits\nbehind it (only `w-72` / `md:w-96` wide when expanded), which is the intended\nbehaviour per the brief. Visual layout is unchanged.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n\nid: lot\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the library search overlay intercepting clicks on the header buttons\n(Filter / Releases / Recommender / genre-edit / Create / ViewSwitcher) while\nthe search is open. The overlay container in `Search.svelte` was\n`absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center` — a full-width, transparent layer\nfloating above the header row. It had no background, so the buttons stayed\nvisible, but it swallowed every click across the header width.\n\nThe fix makes the overlay container click-through (`pointer-events-none`) and\nrestores pointer events only on the search input and the close button\n(`pointer-events-auto`). The input itself still blocks clicks on whatever sits\nbehind it (only `w-72` / `md:w-96` wide when expanded), which is the intended\nbehaviour per the brief. Visual layout is unchanged.\n\nTASK-1: CSS-class-only change in `Search.svelte`.\nTASK-2: Verified via `npm run check` (0 errors / 0 warnings), Live\n  hit-testing with Playwright + headless chromium at desktop (1280px) and\n  mobile (375px) widths, and inspection of the built CSS.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte`\n  - Search-overlay container (`div.absolute.z-30.flex.w-full.justify-center`,\n    renders when `library.searchVisible` is true): added `pointer-events-none`\n    so clicks pass through the full-width transparent container to the header\n    buttons underneath.\n  - Search `<input>`: added `pointer-events-auto` so the input itself stays\n    interactive (typing, focusing) and continues to block clicks on anything\n    directly behind its own footprint.\n  - Close button (`<IconCircleX />`, `ml-[-30px]` overhang): added\n    `pointer-events-auto` so it stays clickable.\n  - No change to `w-full`, input widths, z-indices, or any visual styling.\n\nTASK-2: Verification only — no code change.\n  - `npm run check` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n  - `npm run build` → the Vite transform + Tailwind CSS generation complete\n    (`✓ built`, all 1961 modules), and the generated app CSS contains both\n    `pointer-events-auto` and `pointer-events-none` utilities. The final\n    adapter-node output step is OOM-killed in this environment (2 GB cgroup\n    memory limit); this is a pre-existing environment constraint, unrelated to\n    the change (the changed files compile cleanly and the client build output\n    is produced).\n  - Playwright hit-test verification (replicating the exact Header + Search\n    overlay structure): with the overlay open at 1280px and 375px,\n    * Filter / Create buttons on both sides of the centered input receive\n      clicks (click propagates through the overlay container),\n    * the close button receives clicks,\n    * a button positioned directly under the expanded input does NOT receive\n      clicks (correct blocking behaviour),\n    * typing into the input works,\n    * computed `pointer-events` = `none` on the container, `auto` on input and\n      close button.\n  - `npm test`: 723/724 pass; the single failure is a pre-existing, unrelated\n    failure in `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts`\n    (`StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes` — expects a\n    `.bg-blue-50` class which Tailwind v4 does not generate as a static\n    utility; the assertion exists in HEAD, untouched by this job).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- `npm run build` cannot complete the final adapter-node server output in this\n  environment due to a 2 GB cgroup memory limit (the process is OOM-killed\n  during app-wide chunk rendering). CI / machines with more memory complete\n  it. Not caused by and not addressable from this change.\n- Pre-existing test failure in `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts`\n  (`StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes`, expecting\n  `.bg-blue-50`) — unrelated to the libraries search bar; already failing\n  before this job.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":75,"totalLines":75,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791624166641,"end":1791624166752}},"id":"prt_1251f3c8e0015tCG7bheYUSRsk","sessionID":"ses_edae0eac3ffeMK1M7G94zFEyN9","messageID":"msg_1251f364e001Cpd7jjR4AHYDxX"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791624167096,"sessionID":"ses_edae0eac3ffeMK1M7G94zFEyN9","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_ET_b6EotD9iuFcmyeqgfM1w8581","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git diff main...HEAD"},"output":"...output truncated...\n\nFull output saved to: /home/claude/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1251f3d68001FDkRUzNdf0US7N\n\nimestamp\":1791624151680,\"sessionID\":\"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1251ed4d0001gSM2HbS5QSwozZ\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1251ec27f001cZvuJNBWnODuMw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Both tasks are complete. Summary of the work:\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n**TASK-1 — Search overlay click-through fix** (`src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte`)\\n- Added `pointer-events-none` to the full-width overlay container (`absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center`) so clicks pass through it to the header buttons beneath\\n- Added `pointer-events-auto` to the search input and the close (circle-x) button so they stay interactive\\n- The input itself still blocks clicks on what sits behind its own `w-72`/`md:w-96` footprint (intended per brief). No visual/layout change; no new UI strings.\\n\\n**TASK-2 — Verification**\\n- `npm run check` → 0 errors, 0 warnings\\n- Live hit-testing with Playwright + headless chromium (replicating the exact Header/Search structure) at both 1280px and 375px: Filter/Create buttons on both sides of the centered input receive clicks ✓, close button clickable ✓, a button directly under the input stays blocked ✓, typing works ✓, computed `pointer-events` = `none`/`auto` as intended ✓\\n- Built CSS confirms Tailwind emitted both new utilities\\n- `npm test`: 723/724 pass — the 1 failure (`StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes`, expecting `.bg-blue-50`) is pre-existing at HEAD and unrelated\\n\\n## Notes\\n- `npm run build`'s vite phase completes cleanly (all 1961 modules) but the final adapter-node chunk assembly is OOM-killed by this environment's 2 GB cgroup limit — a pre-existing environment constraint, not related to the change (documented in `implementation.md`)\\n- `session.log` is a live harness log appended on every tool call; it was committed last per the established job pattern (it will re-dirty while the session is active, as it did for prior agents)\\n\\nCommits on `fix/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries`: `ee41599` (fix) → `c5eb0d6` (implementation summary) → `ba2fb59`/`57516d6`/`5f17adb` (job artifacts). No pushes, no merges, no other branches touched.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791624139984,\"end\":1791624151674}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791624151776,\"sessionID\":\"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1251f02c2001SNCXovV7bR3UYO\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1251ec27f001cZvuJNBWnODuMw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_edaee7027ffeOfy6SFj11X94rs\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":53224,\"input\":315,\"output\":685,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":52224}},\"cost\":0.000614922}}\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tasks.md b/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tasks.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3c40c43\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tasks.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@\n+# Tasks: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n+\n+id: lot\n+analyst: @analyst\n+date: 2026-10-10\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n+\n+## Root cause\n+\n+`src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte` renders its inline search input\n+inside an absolutely positioned, full-width, transparent container:\n+\n+```\n+<div class=\"absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center\">\n+```\n+\n+When `library.searchVisible` is true, this container floats above the whole header\n+row (the same header that holds Filter / Releases / Recommender / genre-edit /\n+Create buttons, rendered by `libraries/shared/Header.svelte`). The container has no\n+background, so the buttons stay visible, but it intercepts every click across the\n+header width, making them unclickable — exactly what the brief describes.\n+\n+`Search.svelte` is the only inline search implementation for libraries (used only by\n+`shared/Header.svelte`, which all eight library pages route through); the separate\n+`LibrarySearchModal.svelte` is a modal and is not affected.\n+\n+Fix: make the overlay container click-through (`pointer-events-none`) and restore\n+pointer events only on the input and the close button (`pointer-events-auto`). The\n+input itself keeps blocking clicks underneath it (with `inputExpanded`, `w-72` /\n+`md:w-96`), which per the brief is the correct behaviour. Visual layout is unchanged.\n+\n+## Task breakdown\n+\n+TASK-1: In `Search.svelte`, add `pointer-events-none` to the search-overlay container\n+     (`absolute z-30 flex w-full justify-center`) and `pointer-events-auto` to the\n+     search input and to the close (circle-x) button, so only the actual input area\n+     blocks clicks while the search is open and the rest of the header stays clickable.\n+     files: src/lib/components/libraries/shared/Search.svelte\n+     depends: none\n+     risk: low — one-file, CSS-class-only change; no visual or logic change, no new\n+     UI strings (no i18n impact). Also closes the same click-blocking during the\n+     collapsed/fade-in state (`w-0` input) for free.\n+\n+TASK-2: Verify the fix: run `npm run check` (+ `npm run build`) and manually confirm\n+     that with the search open, the header buttons (Filter, Releases, Recommender,\n+     genre edit, Create — desktop and mobile variants) and the ViewSwitcher remain\n+     clickable on both sides of the centered input, at desktop and mobile widths,\n+     and that typing in the input still works and blocks what sits behind it.\n+     files: none (verification only — no code change expected)\n+     depends: TASK-1\n+     risk: low — verification task; jsdom cannot model pointer-event hit-testing, so a\n+     component test would not genuinely validate the click-through, and no such test\n+     exists for this component today.\n+\n+## Notes for the developer\n+\n+- Do not change the container's `w-full`, the input widths, or the z-indices —\n+  the visual layout is intentional (centered search bar over a full-width header).\n+  The only required change is pointer-event behaviour.\n+- An alternative (constraining the container width to the input's width) is a valid\n+  approach but wider-reaching and more fragile across breakpoints (input `w-72` vs\n+  `md:w-96` + the 30px close-button overhang); prefer TASK-1's pointer-events fix.\n+- Re-opening the search by clicking the magnifier icon while the overlay is open is\n+  a no-op and stays harmless after the change.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tokens.json b/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tokens.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7e15669\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/tokens.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"agent\": \"analyst\",\n+    \"attempt\": 1,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-10T09:07:47.4175635Z\",\n+    \"inputTokens\": 40912,\n+    \"outputTokens\": 10347,\n+    \"cacheReadTokens\": 314112,\n+    \"costUSD\": 0.013287336000000002\n+  }\n+]\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md b/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9617c51\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+# Verdict: search bar overlays buttons in libraries\n+\n+id: lot\n+reviewer:\n+date:\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n+\n+## Review\n+\n+<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAI